                                "sense_id": "6a12091e-7852-3e96-b5b1-2416ae2cb8b5",
                                "text": "Where the competition is free, the rivalship of competitors, who are all endeavouring to justle one another out of employment, obliges every man to endeavour to execute his work with a certain degree of exactness."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0dd46557-2ced-47b3-b538-6d942901d10e",
                                "sense_id": "6a12091e-7852-3e96-b5b1-2416ae2cb8b5",
                                "text": "Such was the amiable Frenchman for whom I felt that perfect friendship, that soldier-like fraternity, which we are only capable of in our youth, before we are alive to feelings of rivalship, before irrevocable courses, furrow and divide the field of futurity."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
